          },
          "actions": {
            "value": null
          },
          "category": "ancestry",
          "description": {
            "value": "<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per hour</p>\n<p><strong>Trigger</strong> You attempt a saving throw against an area effect from the tradition matching your magiphage ability.</p>\n<hr />\n<p>You consume the magic of an incoming spell or effect to protect your allies, though you might give yourself indigestion. Attempt a counteract check against the triggering effect; your counteract rank equals half your level (rounded up), and for the roll, use either your class DC – 10 or your spellcasting attribute modifier plus your spellcasting proficiency bonus. If you counteract the triggering effect, you end the effect for all other creatures in the area, but you become @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Sickened]{Sickened 1} as your body struggles to absorb the influx of magic.</p>"
          },
          "frequency": {
            "max": 1,
            "per": "PT1H"
          },
          "level": {
            "value": 9
          },
